Description: Fit, inspect, and extend Dirichlet process mixture models for
    Bayesian nonparametric analysis. The package provides an object-based
    interface for density estimation, clustering, hierarchical modelling, and
    custom mixture specifications. Built-in models include Gaussian,
    multivariate Gaussian, Beta, Exponential, Weibull, hierarchical, and hidden
    Markov model workflows, with compiled C++ sampler implementations for the
    main ordinary mixture models and R implementations for extensible and
    hierarchical workflows. Users can define new mixture kernels by supplying
    likelihood, prior, and posterior-update methods while reusing the package's
    Markov chain Monte Carlo machinery. See Teh (2010)
    <https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/~teh/research/npbayes/Teh2010a.pdf>.
